return array(
	'date_fmt' => 'j F Y',
	'k007931cc' => 'About Shizuka Hearing',
	'k00ab9a15' => 'Here are straightforward answers to common questions about hearing evaluations, device fittings, and appointment preparation. We believe in providing clear clinical information so you feel confident before your visit.',
	'k02f2055e' => 'HEARING CHECK',
	'k030875de' => 'Our team brings together clinical audiologists, tinnitus counsellors, technical specialists, and patient care coordinators. We share a commitment to unhurried consultations, scientific verification, and calm personal care.',
	'k051089ee' => 'Custom musician’s earplugs (pair, incl. impressions)',
	'k0527de00' => 'Meet the audiologists',
	'k09ade260' => 'A fitting here is two visits, not a handover at the counter. We choose a hearing aid for your hearing and for the rooms you actually use, at home, at work, and at a café, and we do not steer you toward a manufacturer. Real-ear measurement places a thin probe tube at the ear so we can see the sound that arrives, and adjust it. You then take loaner devices home for 14 days and wear them where the missed sentences happen. The second visit is for what you noticed. Fitting and real-ear verification, including that trial, is €380. The first two review visits are included.',
	'k0b43e040' => 'Martin, 64',
	'k0c6e7dac' => 'Henrik had lived with persistent high-pitched ringing in his ears for two years, finding quiet evenings and falling asleep particularly stressful. During his 75-minute consultation with Mei Lin Hartmann, Henrik learned the neuroacoustic mechanisms behind his tinnitus and began a structured plan combining ambient sound therapy with gentle daytime acoustic enrichment. Over four weeks of consistent sound exposure and follow-up guidance, the contrast between internal noise and quiet rooms lessened significantly. While his tinnitus has not magically disappeared, Henrik finds it noticeably less intrusive, allowing him to read quietly and sleep soundly through the night.',
	'k0d620a71' => 'Hearing aids sound very different in real-world environments than they do in a quiet consulting room. Our fitting package includes a 14-day home trial using loaner devices programmed to your prescription. Over two weeks, you test the instruments in familiar settings: watching television at home, talking over dinner in noisy restaurants, and walking outside. You maintain a simple listening log noting any environments where speech felt muffled or sharp. At your second fitting visit, we analyze your experiences and refine the acoustic programming to ensure long-term comfort and optimal clarity.',
	'k14674ed6' => 'Before you book',
	'k14b53ddf' => 'AFTERCARE &amp; REVIEW',
	'k14d3cacc' => 'Samuel Okafor',
	'k14e7df5d' => 'We welcome visitors to our quiet, accessible clinic in Northgate. Whether you wish to book a hearing check or attend our free monthly listening evening, our team is here to assist you.',
	'k16c0b6f7' => 'She had stepped out of the choir’s alto row because she could not trust her line against the voices beside her. A hearing aid, fitted with real-ear measurement and tried at home for 14 days, brought her back into rehearsal. She still listens hard when the hall is bright. She is singing in the alto row again. That is her account, not a result we promise to anyone else.',
	'k17d2eeed' => 'Transparent Fees',
	'k1b17a5a6' => 'The year the clinic opened',
	'k1cb4dc75' => 'Our tinnitus care is led by Mei Lin Hartmann, who combines sound therapy strategies with structured acoustic counselling. By introducing gentle background sounds, broadband noise, or soothing natural soundscapes, we can reduce the sharp contrast between your tinnitus and silent environments. This acoustic enrichment helps the auditory cortex de-emphasize internal noise. Alongside sound therapy, Mei Lin provides cognitive reassurance and practical sleep strategies, demystifying the mechanisms behind your symptoms. Understanding why tinnitus occurs reduces the autonomic threat response, allowing your central nervous system to gradually habituate and push the noise into the background of attention.',
	'k1e9892d1' => 'Two visits and a 14-day home trial.',
	'k1fe917b0' => 'FAQ',
	'k230fce78' => 'Six-Month Review and Yearly Checks',
	'k27bd274b' => 'Specialized Care and Reviews',
	'k291aff28' => 'Diagnostic assessment with speech-in-noise test (90 min)',
	'k2e4cfd73' => 'Most adults who book at Harbour Lane are not living in silence. They follow the start of a story at dinner, then lose the name or the joke under the room. Friends think they are distracted. They are working harder than anyone at the table can see. The clinic begins with that ordinary strain. A hearing check, a speech-in-noise test, and a fitting verified at the ear are all arranged around conversation, rather than around a device on its own. You should leave knowing what was measured and when we will look again. We do not send you out on a promise.',
	'k31aa8e36' => 'Founder and clinical audiologist',
	'k32b02f2f' => 'Fitting Method',
	'k33080c3d' => 'ABOUT',
	'k343f644a' => 'Habituation is a gradual process that requires ongoing support, reassurance, and periodic acoustic adjustments. Following your initial consultation, we arrange a structured follow-up appointment at four weeks to evaluate your progress. During this review, Mei Lin assesses how your sleep patterns and daytime concentration have responded to sound therapy devices or ambient noise strategies. We refine sound generator levels, address any lingering questions, and adapt your personalized care plan to ensure steady comfort. Our commitment is to provide ongoing guidance so that sound perception ceases to dominate your daily life and quiet moments feel calm again.',
	'k354093c5' => '18 Harbour Lane, Northgate<br>2nd floor, lift access from the street<br>Tram stop Harbour Lane, 3 minutes’ walk',
	'k360a036f' => 'Inside our sound booth, we conduct pure-tone audiometry to map the softest pitches you can hear across low, mid, and high frequencies. Because everyday life rarely occurs in total silence, we follow pure-tone testing with an essential speech-in-noise evaluation. During this test, you listen to spoken sentences presented against varying levels of competing background noise. This measurement reveals how effectively your auditory system separates speech from surrounding chatter, pinpointing the real-world strain you experience at dinner tables or social gatherings. The diagnostic assessment provides the objective evidence needed to guide appropriate care.',
	'k37a98c48' => 'Selecting a hearing aid begins by examining your audiogram, the physical contours of your ear canal, and your personal lifestyle needs. Rather than promoting specific brands or trendy aesthetics, we focus entirely on acoustic performance, comfort, and ease of handling. We discuss whether discreet behind-the-ear models or compact in-the-ear styles suit your hearing profile and manual dexterity. We also review practical considerations such as rechargeable cases and streaming capabilities. Our objective is to find a device that matches your acoustic requirements, supports speech comprehension in noisy settings, and feels comfortable throughout full days of wear.',
	'k37abe107' => 'What happens during a 60-minute hearing check?',
	'k38d2c59d' => 'Hearing aid cleaning and re-tune (30 min)',
	'k39dd4613' => 'AUDIOLOGISTS',
	'k3aa4bf27' => 'The proof · 2 weeks, 6 weeks, 6 months',
	'k3b44fee4' => 'Adapting to newly audible sounds takes patience as your auditory cortex relearns how to process background noise and vocal nuances. Our aftercare process begins with a review visit at 2 weeks, followed by a second visit at 6 weeks. Tomás Reyes and our clinical team evaluate your wear logs, examine physical comfort within the ear canal, and listen carefully to your listening experiences at home, at work, and in social settings. We make precise acoustic adjustments to volume and frequency balance. The first two review visits are included with every fitting, providing thorough clinical support as you settle into natural hearing.',
	'k3bb75a08' => 'How do I know if I need a hearing check?',
	'k3ca68fc9' => '2 weeks, 6 weeks, 6 months',
	'k3d6b65cb' => 'What Is Included',
	'k3dbae2c6' => 'JOURNAL',
	'k3e67d49b' => 'OUR APPROACH',
	'k3fca9c6a' => 'Our comprehensive sixty-minute hearing check is designed for adults who find themselves straining to follow conversation in lively rooms. We look beyond standard beeps to measure how clearly you understand speech when background sound is present.',
	'k409dfb8e' => 'THE REVIEW VISIT',
	'k411532a4' => 'THE FITTING',
	'k411e68a2' => 'Audiologist and fitting lead',
	'k4272078b' => 'Shizuka Hearing has kept the same address since it opened in 2014: 18 Harbour Lane, Northgate, on the second floor, with a lift from the street. Dr. Elena Varga left a hospital ENT department to build a clinic in which a fitting takes the time it needs, and the rooms are arranged for that pace. Conversation, otoscopy, counselling, and the fitting itself happen in the consulting rooms. The measures that need quiet, including pure-tone audiometry, happen in the sound booth. The entrance is a glass door on a quiet morning street, with no separate test centre to find after the appointment. You come up, you are seen, and the next visit is a date in the same building rather than a referral onward. Tram stop Harbour Lane is a 3-minute walk. Phone +00 555 0184. Email hello@shizuka-hearing.example.',
	'k43a918be' => 'Our complete fitting package costs €380 and includes two dedicated clinic visits alongside a structured 14-day home trial. During your initial fitting visit, we program your chosen loaner devices using real-ear verification and instruct you on handling, cleaning, and daily charging routines. Over the following two weeks, you wear the devices in your actual living environments, including family dinners, neighborhood walks, and noisy café settings. You then return for your second visit, where we evaluate your listening logs, refine frequency settings based on your real-world feedback, and ensure conversation feels natural and clear.',
	'k43a9cac6' => 'The missed sentence is rarely the whole conversation. It is the name at the end of a question, or the aside a friend makes while a restaurant talks over them. You lean in, watch the mouth, and still lose the line. Nodding feels easier than asking again. At Shizuka Hearing the first visit starts with that, not with a device. A hearing check lasts 60 minutes: conversation, a look in the ear, and pure-tone audiometry. When background sound is the real problem, the diagnostic assessment runs 90 minutes and includes a speech-in-noise test. You take home a plain-language summary. The hearing check is €95. The diagnostic assessment is €160.',
	'k44052de4' => 'Hearing checks, fittings, trials and reviews',
