	'k44df529b' => 'Book a hearing check',
	'k47bb3536' => 'The sentence you missed,<br>and every moment it brings back.',
	'k487b0f0d' => 'Located on the second floor at 18 Harbour Lane, Northgate, our clinic is arranged to provide a calm, peaceful atmosphere from the moment you step through the doors. The facility features two dedicated consulting rooms and a purpose-built acoustic sound booth designed for accurate pure-tone and speech-in-noise evaluations. Large windows provide soft natural daylight, creating an airy and welcoming setting for clinical testing and device programming. Lift access ensures step-free arrival for all visitors. We keep appointments spaced generously apart, ensuring our waiting room remains quiet and restful, with ample time reserved for every individual consultation.',
	'k49ee3087' => 'Name',
	'k4bed9b57' => 'Every hearing journey is individual, shaped by unique acoustic environments, personal routines, and social connections. Here, three patients share their experiences of rediscovering clarity in everyday life.',
	'k4c2a8fe7' => 'Message',
	'k4ce9fc11' => 'Clinic Location and Transport',
	'k4cf2cf46' => 'In 2014, Dr. Elena Varga left a hospital ENT department to establish Shizuka Hearing at 18 Harbour Lane in Northgate. Working within hospital constraints, appointments were often rushed, leaving little room to understand how adults actually experience sound in daily life. Dr. Varga set out to create an independent clinic where consultations take the time they truly require. From our earliest consultations, our focus has stayed on helping people who struggle in noisy rooms, dinner parties, and busy family gatherings. We chose a quiet space on the second floor, accessible by lift, where patients could speak openly without feeling hurried or processed.',
	'k4d057203' => 'TINNITUS',
	'k4d5d98a1' => 'How we begin',
	'k4d6c0f83' => 'Listening, sound therapy and follow-up',
	'k4d7b2e17' => 'How often should my hearing aids be serviced and checked?',
	'k4e063509' => 'Claire Dubois',
