	'k563d7152' => '60 minutes, then a plain-language report',
	'k599e6a3a' => 'Cleaning and Technical Maintenance',
	'k5b599674' => 'Two visits and a 14-day home trial',
	'k5df69c0f' => 'Every human ear canal has a unique shape and acoustic resonance, meaning the same hearing aid sound setting behaves differently in two different ears. To eliminate guesswork, we perform real-ear measurement during fitting. We place a soft, hair-thin silicone probe tube inside your ear canal next to the eardrum while the hearing aid is in place. As calibrated speech signals play in the room, external microphones measure the exact sound levels reaching your eardrum. We fine-tune the amplification across individual frequencies in real time, verifying that soft speech becomes audible while loud sounds remain strictly comfortable and safe.',
	'k5e728c78' => 'Martin had gradually withdrawn from his local weekly quiz night at a bustling neighborhood pub. As background clatter and multiple competing voices made trivia questions unintelligible, he found himself nodding politely along rather than joining the banter. After a comprehensive diagnostic assessment at our Northgate clinic revealed high-frequency hearing loss, Samuel Okafor fitted him with discreet devices calibrated through real-ear verification. Following his 14-day trial and 6-week review, Martin returned to his quiz team with renewed ease. He can now follow banter across the table and catch punchlines without feeling exhausted.',
	'k5edde140' => 'Since 2014, second floor, Harbour Lane',
	'k63362f90' => 'Every fee, before you book',
	'k63390fef' => 'Our €380 fitting fee covers the complete clinical onboarding process across two dedicated appointments. It includes objective real-ear probe measurements, individual acoustic programming, loaner devices for your 14-day home trial, and personal instruction on cleaning, handling, and daily charging. Crucially, the fee also covers your first two review visits at 2 weeks and 6 weeks with our audiology team. We ensure your devices are fine-tuned as your brain adapts to sound. Subsequent 45-minute reviews are priced at €60, ensuring ongoing clinical support whenever your hearing needs adjustment.',
	'k64defe9f' => 'What is included in the fitting fee of €380?',
	'k65853b68' => 'At the conclusion of your visit, we discuss all findings with you in clear, plain language without confusing medical jargon. You receive a printed summary of your audiogram and your speech-in-noise results, along with practical explanations of what the numbers mean for your day-to-day communication. If hearing assistance is recommended, we explain suitable options and answer your questions openly. Our standard hearing check takes 60 minutes for €95, while our complete diagnostic assessment with speech-in-noise testing takes 90 minutes for €160. You are never pressured to purchase devices, and all results are yours to keep.',
	'k686dcce2' => 'Sound Therapy and Counselling',
	'k68cb804b' => 'Aftercare and review',
	'k6a2de90b' => 'Many adults notice gradual changes in their hearing long before they experience difficulty in quiet rooms. If you frequently find yourself asking family members to repeat sentences, struggling to follow group conversations in restaurants, or raising the television volume above what others find comfortable, a hearing check is recommended. Missing consonants or feeling mentally fatigued after social gatherings are also classic indicators. Our 60-minute hearing check for €95 provides objective measurements of your hearing sensitivity and clarifies whether your difficulties stem from earwax, auditory fatigue, or high-frequency hearing loss.',
	'k6a7e7316' => 'Hours',
