	'k6e010349' => 'ANSWERS',
	'k7002e723' => 'Today · Open 9:00–18:00 · Next open listening evening Thu 18:30',
	'k732798a2' => 'TEAM',
	'k766c2b05' => 'FITTING METHOD',
	'k77befd2b' => 'Call, write, or send a request',
	'k77d9f794' => 'Book a time that suits you. The clinic is open Monday to Friday, 9:00–18:00, on Thursday until 20:00, and on Saturday from 9:00 to 13:00.',
	'k795512b3' => 'Opening Hours and Listening Evenings',
	'k7bc1ac75' => 'No referral from a general practitioner or ENT specialist is required to schedule an appointment at Shizuka Hearing. You are welcome to contact our clinic directly by phone or via our website booking form. However, if our otoscopic examination or audiometric assessment reveals sudden asymmetric hearing loss, persistent ear pain, active discharge, or unilateral tinnitus, we will immediately recommend medical evaluation by an ear, nose, and throat physician. We regularly collaborate with local healthcare providers and can supply copies of your diagnostic reports upon request.',
	'k7c024c56' => 'We begin every appointment with a detailed conversation about your hearing history, daily routines, and the specific listening environments where speech feels unclear. We explore whether you find yourself asking people to repeat themselves in noisy restaurants, turning up the television volume, or missing parts of family conversations. Following this discussion, your audiologist performs video otoscopy to examine the physical health of your outer ear and eardrum. This gentle visual check identifies any earwax blockage, inflammation, or structural irregularities that might temporarily affect your hearing before we proceed with acoustic testing in the sound booth.',
	'k7e439e22' => 'Priya Nair',
	'k7f54bd91' => 'Persistent ringing, buzzing, or hissing in the ears can be exhausting and distressing. Our dedicated tinnitus consultations offer a calm, evidence-based space to understand your sound perception and rebuild daily peace of mind.',
	'k822c6c6f' => 'Night was the hardest part of the day, because the tinnitus did not drop when the flat went quiet. He came for a 75-minute consultation with Mei Lin Hartmann, with counselling and sound therapy, and a follow-up at 4 weeks. He does not describe a cure. He says the sound is quieter at night than it was, and less in the way of sleep. Many people find it becomes less intrusive. Experiences differ.',
	'k82b68162' => 'Ana, 47',
	'k83120999' => 'Visit and contact',
	'k8434c094' => 'Fitting hearing aids is a precise clinical procedure rather than an over-the-counter transaction. We combine objective acoustic measurements with real-world home trials to ensure sound feels balanced, comfortable, and clear.',
	'k865dbcef' => 'Tinnitus consultation (75 min)',
	'k868bf055' => 'Jonas Lindqvist is our hearing aid technician, responsible for precision acoustic testing, device cleaning, shell modifications, and rapid repairs. Jonas ensures that all instruments, whether during a 14-day home trial or yearly review, meet strict acoustic performance standards. Priya Nair is our patient coordinator, managing front-of-house appointments, patient enquiries, and listening evening schedules. Priya ensures that your arrival at 18 Harbour Lane is smooth, welcoming, and relaxed. From your initial phone call to your long-term annual reviews, our entire staff works together to make your hearing journey reassuring and seamless.',
	'k8740fe7c' => 'What is real-ear measurement and why is it essential?',
	'k88c21a14' => 'Three people, in their own words',
	'k89a810b4' => 'Shizuka Hearing is located on the second floor at 18 Harbour Lane, Northgate. The clinic is easily accessible by public transport, situated just a three-minute walk from the &quot;Harbour Lane&quot; tram stop. For visitors arriving on foot or by car, step-free access is provided via a spacious elevator directly to our second-floor entrance. Our consulting rooms and sound booth are designed with wide doorways to accommodate wheelchairs and walking aids. If you require any additional assistance upon arrival, Priya Nair at our reception desk is always ready to assist you.',
	'k8a2be3b2' => 'Mon–Fri 9:00–18:00<br>Thursday until 20:00<br>Saturday 9:00–13:00<br>Sunday and public holidays closed',
	'k8ba469c6' => 'Reviews at 2 Weeks and 6 Weeks',
	'k8d983a37' => 'Martin, 64 — Quiz Nights Again',
	'k8db1c6b5' => 'Tinnitus counsellor',
	'k911fa328' => 'PRICE LIST',
	'k93a13471' => 'Listening, sound therapy and follow-up.',
	'k945390d8' => 'Audiologist for review visits',
	'k961bb584' => 'Conversation and Otoscopy',
	'k968a327b' => 'QUESTIONS',
	'k96b5e8e6' => 'Quiz nights had become a blur of answers he heard a moment too late, so he stopped putting his hand up. After a hearing check, a fitting verified at the ear, and the review visits that followed, he went back to the table with his friends. He still asks for a repeat when the pub gets loud. He also catches the punchline often enough to stay for the next round. His experience is his own, and experiences differ.',
	'k97eae1cf' => 'Choosing Your Devices',
	'k983054af' => 'Tinnitus Care',
	'k98718a0b' => 'SHIZUKA',
	'k98d9fed3' => 'Technical Support and Coordination',
	'k9913326e' => 'We start from the sentence you missed.',
	'k9b9ae291' => 'Every consultation at Shizuka Hearing includes dedicated one-on-one time with a qualified clinician in a private consulting room or sound booth. When you undertake a hearing check or diagnostic assessment, your fee covers video otoscopy, calibrated pure-tone audiometry, speech-in-noise testing, and a written plain-language report detailing your results. When fitting hearing aids, your €380 fee includes real-ear probe-tube verification, loaner instruments during the 14-day trial, bespoke acoustic tuning, and your first two follow-up review visits at 2 weeks and 6 weeks. You will never encounter hidden facility fees or administrative charges.',
	'k9dea2052' => 'THE SEVEN',
	'k9fce6099' => 'We are an audiology clinic for adults who nod along in restaurants and miss the end of the sentence. We test hearing in noise, fit and verify hearing aids with real-ear measurement, and see you again until conversation feels easy.',
	'ka03e62b4' => 'Real-ear measurement is an objective verification standard that measures the exact sound pressure delivered by a hearing aid directly inside your ear canal. Because ear canals differ significantly in volume, shape, and acoustic resonance, generic manufacturer software settings can miss prescription targets by substantial margins. By placing a tiny silicone probe tube adjacent to your eardrum during fitting, we measure calibrated speech in real time. We adjust your hearing aid&#x27;s frequency response until amplified speech matches your auditory prescription precisely, ensuring that conversation sounds natural, intelligible, and comfortable in daily wear.',
